# Deploy workflow

When finishing a change that should go to production:

1. Commit relevant files (never `.env`, secrets, `*.db` test dumps).
2. Push to `origin/main` on GitHub.
3. Always end with the Timeweb SSH command.

Default Timeweb command:

```bash
cd /opt/tehnikagoda && git pull origin main && docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml up --build -d
```

If `.env` on the server must change too, include those `sed`/`echo` steps in the same one-liner before or with the pull/rebuild.

Do not wait for the user to ask "залить" — do commit + push + Timeweb command by default after production-ready work, unless they say not to.
